(ii) $C$ cannot be completely covered with $25$ pieces of shape (b);

(iii) $C$ cannot be completely covered with $25$ pieces of shape (c).

ar.2025.0.1.reviewed_statement:
Find all pairs $(p, q)$ of positive primes, not necessarily distinct, such that the expression $p^2 + 3pq + q^2$ is

(a) a perfect square;

(b) a power of $5$.

vn.1985.1.2.reviewed_statement:
Find all functions $f : \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{R}$ satisfying:
