(c) the locus, as $p$ varies, of the intersection points $P$ of the parallels through $A'$ and $C'$ to the sides $AB$ and $AC$ respectively.

rs.2020.1.2.reviewed_statement:
A polyhedron with at least $5$ vertices is given, in each of whose vertices exactly three edges meet. Prove that it is possible to assign to each vertex of the polyhedron a rational number so that the following conditions are satisfied:

