gra.1996.0.2.reviewed_statement:
Let $ABC$ be an acute triangle, $AD$, $BE$, $CZ$ its altitudes and $H$ its orthocentre. Let $AI$ and $A\Theta$ be the internal and external bisectors of the angle $A$. Let $M$, $N$ be the midpoints of $BC$, $AH$, respectively. Prove that:

